<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  NOTE ON THE ROOT ELEMENT.

  This file's root is <Patch>, not <Defs>. Every patch file this mod previously shipped
  (NPCEquipment_Removal.xml and the three .disabled files) used <Defs> as the root, which
  means RimWorld loaded them as def files and tried to construct a def type called
  "Operation". None of them ever ran. That is why the "player-exclusive" behaviour and the
  trader stock injection never worked in game.

  Patches only run from a <Patch> root inside a Patches/ folder.
-->
<Patch>

  <!--
    Register the DMC caravan trader with the outlander factions.

    A TraderKindDef with <orbital>false</orbital> is only ever selected for a trade caravan
    if some FactionDef names it in <caravanTraderKinds>. DMC_LegendaryWeaponCaravan was
    defined but listed nowhere, so it could not spawn. Its own <commonality>0.08</commonality>
    keeps it rare relative to the four vanilla outlander caravans.

    TARGET THE ABSTRACT BASE, NOT THE CONCRETE FACTIONS.

    Patches run against the raw XML document, before ParentName inheritance is resolved.
    OutlanderCivil and OutlanderRough do not declare <caravanTraderKinds> themselves - they
    inherit it from the abstract FactionDef Name="OutlanderFactionBase" (Core,
    Factions_Misc.xml line 57). An xpath aimed at the concrete defs therefore matches
    nothing and the operation fails, which is exactly what happened on the first attempt.

    One operation on the base covers both: OutlanderCivil is a direct child, and
    OutlanderRough reaches it through OutlanderRoughBase. Neither redeclares the list, so
    both inherit the added entry.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[@Name="OutlanderFactionBase"]/caravanTraderKinds</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>DMC_LegendaryWeaponCaravan</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    No NPC-equipment removal patch is needed any more.

    The old one tried to strip a weaponTag called DMCWeapon out of vanilla PawnKindDefs -
    but no vanilla pawnkind has ever asked for that tag, so even a working version of that
    patch would have removed nothing. The weapons leaked to raiders because they *also*
    carried MedievalMeleeDecent / MedievalMeleeAdvanced (melee) and
    SimpleGun / Pistol / Revolver / Autopistol (ranged), which are precisely the tags
    mercenary, tribal, Empire, Traders Guild and outlander pawnkinds roll from.

    Those tags are now gone from the weapon defs themselves, which is a stronger guarantee
    than a patch: there is nothing left to strip.
  -->

</Patch>
